  designNotes: "Beat 6: stage boss. Default squad is 6 rifle + 2 rocket — the keep
    is the first masonry the player is handed the tool for. The first BossPhaseTrigger the project has ever
    fired \u2014 the keep falling spawns the Citadel Sovereign (160 hp) and a heavy,
    so the level does not end when the structure does. Biome reuses Mountains
    from beat 1 on purpose: same ground, a fortress instead of a hut, which is the
    clearest possible read on how far the player has come. Structure hp RETUNED 2026-08-07:
    bunker and keep both hpScale 0.66 (180 -> 118, 212 -> 139), garrisoned total
    392 -> 257. Scaled TOGETHER so the keep stays the dominant structure; 257 leaves
    a stage boss less slack than the levels before it, which is the point. BOSS SPAWN MOVED 2026-08-12: the heavy escort was at anchorX 3 and TWO of its
    three men stood inside MountainBunker's box (x[0.88,3.13]) - the bunker is NOT this phase's
    trigger, so it is still standing when they arrive and they could not be hit. Escort moved to
    4.5 and the Sovereign from 5 to 6.5 so the two groups do not stand on each other. Both now
    land in the KEEP's footprint, which is rubble by definition at that moment - the keep is
    what triggers the phase - so they emerge from the breach, which is what the beat wanted
    anyway. Found because rule 8 was extended to mid-battle arrivals; it had only ever measured
    turn 0. BOSS ESCORT 3->1 AND TELEGRAPH WITHDRAWN 2026-09-05: Rob, playing the now-visible
    boss, said L6 is still hard and he does not like the banner. The garrison half is
    untouched. The spike was 260 hp + 3x64 hp heavies shooting 38/turn into a spent army;
    two of the three escorts were the lever that is both HP and outgoing damage. The
    Sovereign stayed 260 until 2026-09-05: played L6, garrison half easy, then five AP
    volleys into the boss phase with zero kills. 260 is four clean rifle volleys if they
    all land on him; a spent army cannot trade that. HP 260 -> 160 (2.5x a heavy, two
    volleys of eight rifles). Same definition on L12 \u2014 the finale still has the four
    charging shields. Empty telegraphLabel is deliberate \u2014 the
    keep falling IS the warning, and a strip that spoils that is worse than a blindside.
    WRECK Z 2026-09-06: rule 10 had been measuring the collapse clip's REST pose (keep MaxZ 0.51).
    The last frame of collapse throws the pile to z 1.68, so the bosses at 0.9 stood behind
    the rubble on device. Sample the held frame; bosses 0.9 -> 2.1. Dirt trio 2.25 -> 1.70
    (heavies 0.8 -> 0.35) so two of three are not inside the bunker's collapsed splat (minX 2.08)."
